{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/665974-what-crosses-between-the-umbra-and-the-physical-world","id":665974,"title":"What crosses between the Umbra and the physical world","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-15T12:41:55-07:00","id":665974,"title":"What crosses between the Umbra and the physical world","content":"I'm nowhere near my books and I need a quick answer. What crosses through to the spirit world and back? One example: If a Garou dies in the Umbra, can his packmates carry him back? Can a corpse even remain in the Umbra as a corpse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:45:53-07:00","id":665994,"title":"","content":"Yes, a corpse can remain as a corpse in the Umbra. Given that the Garou in question is no longer alive, the pack can also retrieve the body without need of a Gift, since it's still technically half-spirit and half-flesh and can be carried though like a fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:23:42-07:00","id":666032,"title":"","content":"I'm imaging the transition from a Garou's death to becoming an ancestor spirit. In a way, I want to say the body dying in the Umbra becomes an ancestor spirit by going into Slumber, fading to the deeps and reappearing where it belongs, like a tribal homeland or Gaia herself to be recycled as it were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T20:00:42-07:00","id":666345,"title":"","content":"No, a garou corpse is just a dead body. There is no indication, that it is half spirit. And, unlike a fetish there is no concious spirit inhabiting it, neither is there spirit essence imbued into it, like with a Talen. Fact is, garou can't bring the body back into the material world. They would need the assistance of a spirit with an appropriate charm or a glass walker with the athro level gift &quot;Tractor beam&quot;. Since both aren't usually available, it might be necessary to travel in the penumbra to the nearest caern an hope the ritemaster there allows that the corpse be brought back in the heart of the caern, where the Gauntlet has a rating of 0.<br /> <br /> If not done in a relatively large window of time, I'd assume, the body might dissolve, just like epherma dissolves in the material world.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Also, one could theoretically use the Rite of Talisman Dedication in the corpse, but I'd see it as a misuse of the Rite that should rise the difficulty (as of Tribebook: Bone Gnawers Rite Improvising Sidebar) and result in renown loss.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, dead garou don't become ancestor spirits. Ancestor spirits are the personification of what a certain tribe, breed or auspice embodies. They may take the form of, and act like notable dead garou, but they aren't their souls or something like that. If a garou dies, their souls goes to Gaia - unless their connection with gaia is severed in some way (usually through sins). If that is the case the garou might become a wraith. But if not, he goes the way all mortals go in the world of darkness and that is either Transcendence or Oblivion. The End.<br /> <br /> If a soul of a garou, that return to gaia, is then &quot;turned&quot; into a new garou (leading to the believe of reincarnation and Past Live as prominent evident in the Stargazer tribe) or if they just stay part of the greater universe - to be taped in via the Ancestors background is not specifically mentioned in the books. Point is, they could be ancestor spirits, if Gaia chooses them to become such, but it is not a given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 09-15-2015, 11:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T04:36:28-07:00","id":666707,"title":"","content":"Where are you digging up that information on what happens to Garou souls?<br /> <br /> All the stories ancestor spirits have to say and the fact that one of them is Wepauwet who has an excellent grasp on his history point to them actually being your Ancestors. That's quite in theme with the whole family thing of Garo, and it just gives an additional impetus for the Garou to know that they are truly walking in the shoes of their forefathers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T05:09:13-07:00","id":666759,"title":"","content":"Wepauwet is not an ancestor spirit like other ancestor spirits. If I'm not mistaken he was subject to the &quot;Spell of Life&quot; that would turn a human into a mummy. But as a garou the spell worked differently on him, turning him into a being that suffers damage when in the physical world. So he retreated to the umbra an became a disconnected being. The only other Silent Strider ancestor spirits in the books (Umbra revised iirc) are also disconnected garou. Meaning, that they fell victim to the rule that the difficulty to step sideways is raised for each year in the Umbra until return is impossible, turning the garou into a spirit being that most garou would regard as ancestor spirit.<br /> <br /> The information on garou not becoming wraith was in Ghost Towns, I think, but I couldn't find it on the fly. The information that ancestor spirits aren't necessarily dead garou is in the ancestor spirit description in both 2nd and revised. Basically stating that it is believed in the game world, but not undisputed.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Their uniqueness made Wepauwet and these other two Striders bypass the Curse that was placed on the Silent Strider tribe. If Wepauwet was a regular ancestor spirit, he would be with the other ancestor spirits at what ever place they were banished to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}